<title>GERMANY: BOE's Davies - French, German news adds to EMU doubt.</title>
<headline>BOE's Davies - French, German news adds to EMU doubt.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of England Deputy Governor Howard Davies said on Friday recent developments in France and Germany were adding to uncertainity about the start of European monetary union (EMU) on time in January 1999.</p>
<p>Davies said the German fight between the Bundesbank and Bonn over the valuation of central bank assets and the left wing's victory in France's recent election were the key factors that were adding to the uncertainity.</p>
<p>He also said at a Bundesbank conference in Frankfurt that Britain's &quot;wait and see&quot; policy on joining EMU was justified and said nations seeking to join the currency must show convergence on the criteria on a sustainable basis.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
